From 2e41aca23b83ede6c4d9b2febb276ae7fe760f9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178 <ms178@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 23:36:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] i686: keep the multilib GCC include dir on the -m32
 search path

set_target("i686") filtered every system include path containing
"x86_64", including /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/<v>/include. On
Debian/Ubuntu multilib layouts that directory is shared between -m32
and -m64 and is exactly what real `gcc -m32` puts on its search path:
stddef.h, stdarg.h, stdatomic.h and the (macro-guarded) intrinsic
headers live there and are word-size-agnostic. Dropping it left every
i686 hosted build that includes <stdio.h> or any GCC-provided header
failing with "stddef.h: No such file or directory".

Keep /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-*/ include dirs; still filter the x86-64 C
library dirs (glibc's /usr/include/x86_64-linux-gnu bits and
/usr/x86_64-linux-gnu/include), whose 64-bit-only headers must not be
seen by -m32 compiles. Dedicated i686/gcc-cross i686 dirs are still
probed first, so Fedora/Arch native-i686 and cross layouts are
unchanged.

Verified: <stdio.h>-based trampoline probe now compiles and runs on
i686 with results identical to `gcc -m32` (f0(f2,&i)=8; trailing i
differs only by unspecified argument evaluation order); GCC-include
headers resolve; dedicated-i686 layouts unaffected (candidates still
probed in the same order).
