From 38d06c717174f31438a85c79eea8e4c70ecb602f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178 <ms178@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:03:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] aarch64: peephole spill-slot threading + adrp remat CSE
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two new fixpoint passes over the RA's residual asm artifacts:

Pass 6 — spill-slot threading (CCC_NO_SPILL_THREAD): rewrite
  str xS,[sp,#off] ... clobber xS ... ldr xD,[sp,#off]
into a caller-saved scratch thread (mov xR,xS / mov xD,xR) whenever the
function-wide census proves the offset has no other reference. The store
is deleted only then; windows end at labels/calls/pair ops, partial-word
stores inside the slot's 8 bytes block (the aggregate_copy_forward overlap
family — an exact-token census is unsound), and x18-x30 destinations are
never paired (their loads are ABI home restores; rewritten into Move form
they get deleted by ABI-unaware dead-move passes and the caller's
register is never restored — costaware_devirt segfault class).

Pass 7 — adrp+add rematerialisation CSE (CCC_NO_ADRP_CSE): the RA
rematerialises `adrp xA,sym; add xA,xA,:lo12:sym` per use; a repeated
pair in one block whose canonical register is still intact loses the
second adrp (and the second add for the same register). Def detection is
allowlist-based; anything unrecognised kills all tracked state (a missed
CSE is a missed opt, a wrong one a miscompile). adrp lines are resolved
before kill bookkeeping so a deleted pair cannot invalidate its own
canonical entry.

test_gsf_invalidation_on_reg_overwrite is updated to the strictly
stronger threaded value-flow shape (capture before clobber, use of the
captured original after it, slot fully gone) — the old "the ldr survives"
assertion pinned a weaker, now-superseded form.

Gates: cargo test --lib 1289/0 under -D warnings (+7 new fixtures); full
ARM differential corpus 379/95, identical to the d4283869 baseline minus
nothing (the two residual new names fail on pristine d4283869 too and
arrived with PR #284 / the refreshed cross-toolchain); benchmark corpus
-O2 instruction counts 8686 -> 8630 with 15 programs smaller and none
larger; nested_functions, lea_sib_fold and the 4-backend unroll/stress
differentials stay green.
